  "_declinedReadme": "DATA-01: transaction-state cues, identical to app/lib/engine/parser/transaction_state_cues.dart (drift test: app/test/engine/parser/transaction_state_cues_drift_test.dart) and applied by the same rule in parse.ts isDeclinedText: whole-token match after folding tashkeel/tatweel/hamza/ta marbuta/alef maqsura; a cue right after a stateCueMerchantIntroducers word (except after 'due'/'owing'), optionally followed by one stateCueMerchantNameWords word, is part of a name; a cue next to a stateCueGenericNouns plural (English after it, Arabic before it) or in a question is not a status, unless the noun is followed by a colon or a count (a status header: 'Declined transactions: 1. …'); a cue preceded in its clause (sentence, or after a comma/colon) by a stateCueHypotheticalMarkers entry is not a status; a declinedExemptKeywords credit counts only when not negated, promised, or followed later in its sentence by a declined status that is not attributive (next to a stateCueTransactionNouns/stateCueGenericNouns word), and when it comes before the first declined status. A stateCueReversalWords status in a message naming a stateCuePurchaseNouns word, with no declined cue ('Purchase of SAR 100 at X reversed'), is ambiguous and also not completed (review, no total change). V1-RES3: a declined status counts even after a done credit (a refund of a declined original is review); a declined cue right after a stateCueNegationMarkers word ('not declined') is not a status; a feminine Arabic cue after an Arabic stateCueMerchantNameWords word is a status; the question rule applies only when the question mark ends the cue's own clause; a spaced dash ends a clause; a stateCueFutureMarkers-only clause that names an amount ('Payment of SAR 100 will be declined') does not make a declined cue hypothetical. A not-completed message is treated like ignoreKeywords (rejected, no AI). ignoreKeywords: a Latin word matches only as a whole word with an optional s/es/al/ed/ing ending; Arabic phrases and URL prefixes by substring.",
